  "claims": [
    "Circle Tangent supports two/three curve or free-point contacts, radius locks after the first contact or through the third Radius getter, and FromFirstPoint. Two free points with a locked radius use the final point as center direction.",
    "Native two-curve Enter holds the second contact and seam; FromFirstPoint holds the first. Parallel supports use the first seam and second positional seed. Mixed point constraints and reversed curve directions retain the measured frame rules.",
    "All 26 successful native workflows and one picked-source cancellation compare full NURBS controls, weights, knots, domain, length, closed status, preserved source geometry and selection, and actual Undo/Redo through command and frontend paths on default and native-smlib backends at absolute 1e-6.",
    "The native corpus covers line and circle supports, three tangencies, mixed contacts, parallel supports, reversed directions, preselection, rotated spatial CPlanes, and periodic/clamped Deformable output.",
    "The shared solver reuses existing analytic curve derivatives, circle/arc constructors, closest-point queries and nalgebra SVD. A normalized damped Newton solve enforces contact distance, plane, tangent and optional radius equations; physical residual checks gate acceptance.",
    "Local checks cover spatial and scaled constraints, curved and quadratic NURBS supports, incompatible radii, singular corner seeds, and the incoming tangent at a closed curve endpoint.",
    "Interactive curve and surface-edge routes resolve locations from viewport pointers. Captured source snapshots reject replacement, removal, hiding, locking and changed document tolerance. Previews and source acquisition leave the model and selection unchanged.",
    "The input state machine is shared by frontend and canonical command replay. Failed construction commands preserve the document, preferences and history. Cancellation and command interruption release the session.",
    "Circle, Ellipse, common point input, drafting and component regressions, workspace all-feature lint, formatting and bounded Python protocols pass."
  ],
  "input_calibration": {
    "source": "Public RhinoViewport.ClientToWorld pixel ray intersected with the current construction plane, followed by the authored source curve ClosestPoint. Coordinates and parameters are saved in input_trace.clicks.",
    "policy": "Tests replace only authored input pick positions with these resolved input coordinates. Expected output geometry never participates. Production requests and raw observations are preserved.",
    "spatial_view": "Fresh tilted-plane captures use the public SetToPlanView API and record aligned_construction_plane_view=true before computing pixels.",
    "scope": "Planar guide captures with the recorded view/CPlane; physical pixel aperture parity and arbitrary perspective/nonplanar picks are unqualified."
  },
